A||N||4||Nyte||HOW hard is it to swap 3.4 into an '84?||||6||
Z||000000||Nyte||03-26-2001||01:44 PM||||Ya I always hear about the rewiring and sometimes even bolting holes (is that true?).  But exactly how hard is it really?<P>Don't tell me to just go buy a later year car because I just want to work with what I got and plus I don't want to shell out another $1000-$2000.<P>Also I have the time so that's not a factor.  Dang car is just sittin' in the garage and I go and sit in it at least every day.<P>Also include some monetary facts too.<P>Thanks guys!||||reg||6
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-26-2001||06:10 PM||||Just get a FULL wiring harness for an 86-88 and the fuel lines because they are run different.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nyte||03-27-2001||05:20 AM||||How much is stuff like that going to cost?<P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"||||reg||6
Z||000003||Oreif||03-27-2001||11:33 AM||||You will need the full harness, fuel lines, and I think coolant tubes. As for cost, I would say your best bet would be to find a donor car. Either that someone has or at a junk yard. We were doing a lot of work on a car once. We found a donor at the junkyard and worked out a deal with them. Since we had lots of parts to get, We dis-assembled the car and gave them the pieces which we didn't need and they gave us a discount on the parts we did need. (basically we stripped the car for them but took what we needed) To get the harness you'll need to basically gut the car. Or buy a junkyard chassis, strip it out and give it back to them. Probably cost around $500. (my conservative guess)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||03-27-2001||03:15 PM||||You'll also need to replace the fuel pump. That's another 80 USD for a '96 Corvette pump.<P>And you'll need a clutch (or an appropriate flexplate). And a V6 front mount bracket.<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
